PRE-REGISTRATION -- coach replication                           2026-09-12
Written BEFORE the run. Every finding so far comes from ONE catalogue
(ayoai-mind, 145 skills). Coach is the real deployment and the standing
directive is to test hypotheses against it, so this asks whether the findings
are about catalogues in general or about that one.

MEASURED ON-BOX BEFORE ANY MODEL CALL (counts only crossed the wire)
  coach: 64 skills with a description; FULL 36,930 ch (~8,649 tok),
         FIRST 14,547 ch, NAMES 1,177 ch; 3 families of >=3 covering 25 skills
         (39% of the catalogue); largest family 15; all 64 yield 3 queries.
  ayoai-mind for comparison: 145 skills, 97,907 ch, 36% in >=3 families,
         largest family 15.
  So coach is 38% the SIZE but has HIGHER sibling density. That already
  falsifies "the sibling ceiling is an artifact of an unusually large
  catalogue" -- recorded here because it was measured before the arms ran.

PREDICTIONS, fixed before data
  P1 ALL ARMS SCORE HIGHER than on ayoai-mind. A 64-way choice is easier than a
     145-way one. If they do NOT, catalogue SIZE is not the driver and something
     about coach's skills is harder.
  P2 NAMES STILL COLLAPSES, but by less than the 37.6pp measured on ayoai-mind:
     64 names are more separable than 145.
  P3 FIRST STILL LOSES TO FULL. Direction only -- the magnitude is genuinely
     uncertain and I am not predicting it. Fewer candidates need less
     disambiguation (argues smaller gap); higher sibling density needs more
     (argues larger). Naming both arguments in advance so neither can be
     retrofitted as "what I expected".

DECISION RULES
  PRIMARY: does the RETRACTION replicate? Paired bootstrap over SKILLS on
    (FULL - FIRST), two-sided 95% CI.
      CI excludes zero, positive -> the retraction holds on the real deployment.
      CI includes zero -> the retraction is catalogue-specific; ADR-0155's
        fourth addendum must be scoped to "measured on a 145-skill catalogue"
        rather than stated generally. That is a correction I will make.
      CI excludes zero, negative -> FIRST BEATS FULL on coach; the retraction
        is wrong for the deployment that matters and must be revisited entirely.
  SECONDARY: NAMES vs FULL, same machinery, for P2.
  CONTROL: FULL must clear 45%, same floor as the TOPK run and far from any
    observed value (guard-5645). Empty completions abort (guard-6562).

METHOD CONSTRAINTS
  Runs ON zc-03. Coach's skill text never crosses the wire; only scores do.
  The script sources /etc/zakcode/.env on-box for pod credentials -- the key is
  never printed, never logged, never copied.
  Identical extraction, rendering, scoring and clustering as the 420-query
  ayoai-mind run, so the two are directly comparable. 64 skills x 3 queries =
  192 queries, 576 requests.
